{"annotationScore": 4.0, "comments": [{"commentType": "FUNCTION", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "id": "P01019", "source": "UniProtKB"}], "value": "Essential component of the renin-angiotensin system (RAS), a potent regulator of blood pressure, body fluid and electrolyte homeostasis"}]}, {"commentType": "FUNCTION", "molecule": "Angiotensin-2", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "id": "P01015", "source": "UniProtKB"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "id": "P01019", "source": "UniProtKB"}], "value": "Acts directly on vascular smooth muscle as a potent vasoconstrictor, affects cardiac contractility and heart rate through its action on the sympathetic nervous system, and alters renal sodium and water absorption through its ability to stimulate the zona glomerulosa cells of the adrenal cortex to synthesize and secrete aldosterone. Acts by binding to angiotensin receptors AGTR1 and AGTR2. Also binds the DEAR/FBXW7-AS1 receptor"}]}, {"commentType": "FUNCTION", "molecule": "Angiotensin-3", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "id": "P01019", "source": "UniProtKB"}], "value": "Stimulates aldosterone release"}]}, {"commentType": "FUNCTION", "molecule": "Angiotensin 1-7", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "id": "P11859", "source": "UniProtKB"}], "value": "Is a ligand for the G protein-coupled receptor MAS1. Has vasodilator and antidiuretic effects. Has an antithrombotic effect that involves MAS1-mediated release of nitric oxide from platelets"}]}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "id": "P01019", "source": "UniProtKB"}], "id": "SL-0243", "value": "Secreted"}}]}, {"commentType": "PTM", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "id": "P01019", "source": "UniProtKB"}], "value": "In response to low blood pressure, the enzyme renin/REN cleaves angiotensinogen to produce angiotensin-1. Angiotensin-1 is a substrate of ACE (angiotensin converting enzyme) that removes a dipeptide to yield the physiologically active peptide angiotensin-2. Angiotensin-1 and angiotensin-2 can be further processed to generate angiotensin-3, angiotensin-4. Angiotensin 1-9 is cleaved from angiotensin-1 by ACE2 and can be further processed by ACE to produce angiotensin 1-7, angiotensin 1-5 and angiotensin 1-4. Angiotensin 1-7 has also been proposed to be cleaved from angiotensin-2 by ACE2 or from angiotensin-1 by MME (neprilysin) (By similarity)"}]}, {"commentType": "PTM", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "id": "P01019", "source": "UniProtKB"}], "value": "The disulfide bond is labile. Angiotensinogen is present in the circulation in a near 40:60 ratio with the oxidized disulfide-bonded form, which preferentially interacts with receptor-bound renin (By similarity)"}]}, {"commentType": "SIMILARITY", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Belongs to the serpin family"}]}, {"commentType": "SEQUENCE CAUTION", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "note": "Extended N-terminus.", "sequence": "AAG29056.1", "sequenceCautionType": "Erroneous initiation"}, {"commentType": "SEQUENCE CAUTION", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "note": "Extended N-terminus.", "sequence": "AAG30306.1", "sequenceCautionType": "Erroneous initiation"}], "entryAudit": {"entryVersion": 125, "firstPublicDate": "2003-11-07", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-11-04", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2022-02-23", "sequenceVersion": 2}, "entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "extraAttributes": {"countByCommentType": {"FUNCTION": 4, "PTM": 2, "SEQUENCE CAUTION": 2, "SIMILARITY": 1, "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION": 1}, "countByFeatureType": {"Chain": 1, "Disulfide bond": 1, "Glycosylation": 4, "Peptide": 8, "Sequence conflict": 2, "Signal": 1}, "uniParcId": "UPI001E25D38D"}, "features": [{"description": "", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:000025